---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import ToolCard from '../components/ToolCard.astro';
import WorkflowDiagram from '../components/WorkflowDiagram.astro';
import TryDemo from '../components/TryDemo.astro';
import JsonLd from '../components/JsonLd.astro';
import { getCliMeta } from '../data/registry';

const meta = await getCliMeta();

const jsonLd = {
  '@graph': [
    {
      '@type': 'WebSite',
      '@id': 'https://cli.drbaher.com/#website',
      name: 'contract-ops CLI suite',
      url: 'https://cli.drbaher.com',
      description: 'Nine open-source, local-first CLIs for contract operations — extract, draft, lint, compare, review, convert, sign, and track contracts.',
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Organization',
      '@id': 'https://cli.drbaher.com/#org',
      name: 'contract-ops CLI suite',
      url: 'https://cli.drbaher.com',
      sameAs: ['https://github.com/DrBaher'],
    },
  ],
};
---
<BaseLayout title="Overview" active="overview" description="Nine composable, local-first CLIs built for an agent-first contract workflow: agents do the operational work, humans approve the gates that matter.">
  <JsonLd data={jsonLd} />
  <div class="not-prose hero-band">
    <p class="eyebrow">Built for the agent era</p>
    <h1 class="!mt-2">Agents do the work. You approve what matters.</h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-ink-700 dark:text-night-100 max-w-[62ch]">
      <strong>Nine open-source, local-first CLIs for contract operations</strong> — extract, draft,
      review, lint, compare, convert, sign, and track contracts from the command line. Each works
      standalone; together they cover the whole workflow. Built so an AI agent can run the operational
      work over MCP, while a human approves the gates that matter — starting with signing.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-[12.5px]">
      <span class="rounded-md border border-accent-200 bg-accent-50 px-2 py-1 font-mono text-accent-700 dark:border-accent-700/40 dark:bg-accent-900/20 dark:text-accent-300">MCP-native</span>
      <span class="rounded-md border border-accent-200 bg-accent-50 px-2 py-1 font-mono text-accent-700 dark:border-accent-700/40 dark:bg-accent-900/20 dark:text-accent-300">Hash-chained audit trail</span>
      <span class="rounded-md border border-accent-200 bg-accent-50 px-2 py-1 font-mono text-accent-700 dark:border-accent-700/40 dark:bg-accent-900/20 dark:text-accent-300">Per-signer approval tokens</span>
      <span class="rounded-md border border-accent-200 bg-accent-50 px-2 py-1 font-mono text-accent-700 dark:border-accent-700/40 dark:bg-accent-900/20 dark:text-accent-300">Local-first · MIT</span>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-7">
      <WorkflowDiagram />
    </div>
    <p class="mt-1 text-[14px] text-ink-600 dark:text-night-200 max-w-[74ch]">
      Each box is a separate CLI; the arrows are the handoffs between them — files and JSON in standard
      formats. No proprietary glue, no shared database, no daemon — just standalone tools that compose.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
      <a href="/tour/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-md bg-accent-600 px-4 py-2 text-[14px] font-semibold text-cream-50 shadow-sm transition-colors hover:bg-accent-700 dark:bg-accent-500 dark:text-night-900 dark:hover:bg-accent-400">
        Take the 5-minute tour <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/install/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-md border border-ink-700/15 px-4 py-2 text-[14px] font-medium text-ink-700 transition-colors hover:border-accent-300 hover:text-accent-700 dark:border-night-300/20 dark:text-night-100 dark:hover:text-accent-300">
        Install
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Callout label="TL;DR">
    Nine open-source CLIs, nine repositories, one agent-friendly workflow. Local-first by default —
    no SaaS account, no telemetry, no vendor lock-in. The agent drives via MCP / stdio; the human approves
    signatures and escalations. Use them piecemeal or chain them together.
  </Callout>

  <h2 data-reveal>Nine tools at a glance</h2>

  <div class="not-prose my-5 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-ink-700/10 dark:border-night-300/15" data-reveal>
    <table class="w-full border-collapse text-[14px]">
      <thead>
        <tr class="border-b border-ink-700/15 bg-cream-100 dark:border-night-300/20 dark:bg-night-600">
          <th class="px-4 py-2.5 text-left font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-night-50">Tool</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-2.5 text-left font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-night-50">Stage</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-2.5 text-left font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-night-50">Reads → writes</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="text-ink-800 dark:text-night-100">
        <tr class="border-b border-ink-700/10 dark:border-night-300/15">
          <td class="px-4 py-2.5 align-top"><a href="/tools/extract-cli/" class="font-mono">extract</a> <span class="text-ink-500 dark:text-night-200">· Python</span></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2.5 align-top">Ingest</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2.5 align-top">any contract → structured JSON</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-ink-700/10 dark:border-night-300/15">
          <td class="px-4 py-2.5 align-top"><a href="/tools/template-vault-cli/" class="font-mono">template-vault</a> <span class="text-ink-500 dark:text-night-200">· Python</span></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2.5 align-top">Store</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2.5 align-top">vault → versioned template</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-ink-700/10 dark:border-night-300/15">
          <td class="px-4 py-2.5 align-top"><a href="/tools/draft-cli/" class="font-mono">draft</a> <span class="text-ink-500 dark:text-night-200">· Node</span></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2.5 align-top">Draft</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2.5 align-top">template + params → filled draft</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-ink-700/10 dark:border-night-300/15">
          <td class="px-4 py-2.5 align-top"><a href="/tools/nda-review-cli/" class="font-mono">nda-review</a> <span class="text-ink-500 dark:text-night-200">· Python</span></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2.5 align-top">Review / negotiate</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2.5 align-top">draft → verdict + redlines</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-ink-700/10 dark:border-night-300/15">
          <td class="px-4 py-2.5 align-top"><a href="/tools/contract-lint-cli/" class="font-mono">contract-lint</a> <span class="text-ink-500 dark:text-night-200">· Python</span></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2.5 align-top">Lint gate</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2.5 align-top">one contract → defect findings</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-ink-700/10 dark:border-night-300/15">
          <td class="px-4 py-2.5 align-top"><a href="/tools/compare-cli/" class="font-mono">compare</a> <span class="text-ink-500 dark:text-night-200">· Node</span></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2.5 align-top">Drift gate</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2.5 align-top">two versions → pass / block verdict</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-ink-700/10 dark:border-night-300/15">
          <td class="px-4 py-2.5 align-top"><a href="/tools/docx2pdf-cli/" class="font-mono">docx2pdf</a> <span class="text-ink-500 dark:text-night-200">· Node</span></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2.5 align-top">Convert</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2.5 align-top">.docx → .pdf</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-ink-700/10 dark:border-night-300/15">
          <td class="px-4 py-2.5 align-top"><a href="/tools/sign-cli/" class="font-mono">sign</a> <span class="text-ink-500 dark:text-night-200">· Node</span></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2.5 align-top">Sign</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2.5 align-top">.pdf → signed .pdf + receipt</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2.5 align-top"><a href="/tools/contract-vault-cli/" class="font-mono">contract-vault</a> <span class="text-ink-500 dark:text-night-200">· Python</span></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2.5 align-top">Manage</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2.5 align-top">signed contract → renewals + deadlines</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="text-[13px] text-ink-500 dark:text-night-200" data-reveal>Every tool answers <code class="chip">--catalog json</code> for uniform agent discovery. Exit-code meanings differ per tool — see <a href="/built-for-agents/">built for agents</a>.</p>

  <h2 data-reveal>The tools</h2>

  <div class="not-prose mt-4 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3" data-reveal>
    <ToolCard
      title="extract-cli"
      tagline="Open-loop front door: ingest any contract (.md/.txt/.html/.docx/.pdf) into structured JSON — parties, clauses, dates, governing law — with a confidence and source on every field."
      language="Python"
      install="pipx install extract-cli"
      href="/tools/extract-cli/"
      github="https://github.com/DrBaher/extract-cli"
      icon="/assets/icons/extract-cli.svg"
      version={meta['extract-cli'].version}
      versionSource={meta['extract-cli'].source}
      stars={meta['extract-cli'].stars}
      weeklyDownloads={meta['extract-cli'].weeklyDownloads}
      weeklyDownloadsSource={meta['extract-cli'].weeklyDownloadsSource}
    />
    <ToolCard
      title="template-vault-cli"
      tagline="Git-backed, clause-aware vault for legal-document templates. Fork, swap clauses with recorded provenance, pull upstream upgrades."
      language="Python"
      install="pipx install template-vault-cli"
      href="/tools/template-vault-cli/"
      github="https://github.com/DrBaher/template-vault-cli"
      icon="/assets/icons/template-vault-cli.svg"
      version={meta['template-vault-cli'].version}
      versionSource={meta['template-vault-cli'].source}
      stars={meta['template-vault-cli'].stars}
      weeklyDownloads={meta['template-vault-cli'].weeklyDownloads}
      weeklyDownloadsSource={meta['template-vault-cli'].weeklyDownloadsSource}
    />
    <ToolCard
      title="draft-cli"
      tagline="Fill placeholders in markdown or .docx templates. Typed/computed/positional params, parties registry, multi-doc bundles."
      language="Node.js"
      install="npm i -g @drbaher/draft-cli"
      href="/tools/draft-cli/"
      github="https://github.com/DrBaher/draft-cli"
      icon="/assets/icons/draft-cli.svg"
      version={meta['draft-cli'].version}
      versionSource={meta['draft-cli'].source}
      stars={meta['draft-cli'].stars}
      weeklyDownloads={meta['draft-cli'].weeklyDownloads}
      weeklyDownloadsSource={meta['draft-cli'].weeklyDownloadsSource}
    />
    <ToolCard
      title="nda-review-cli"
      tagline="Draft, review, and negotiate NDAs against your own house playbook. Deterministic by default; opt-in LLM augmentation."
      language="Python"
      install="pipx install nda-review-cli"
      href="/tools/nda-review-cli/"
      github="https://github.com/DrBaher/nda-review-cli"
      icon="/assets/icons/nda-review-cli.svg"
      version={meta['nda-review-cli'].version}
      versionSource={meta['nda-review-cli'].source}
      stars={meta['nda-review-cli'].stars}
      weeklyDownloads={meta['nda-review-cli'].weeklyDownloads}
      weeklyDownloadsSource={meta['nda-review-cli'].weeklyDownloadsSource}
    />
    <ToolCard
      title="contract-lint-cli"
      tagline="Pre-signature quality gate: lint one contract for internal-consistency defects — leftover placeholders, broken cross-references, defined-term and numbering issues — with CI-gateable exit codes."
      language="Python"
      install="pipx install contract-lint"
      href="/tools/contract-lint-cli/"
      github="https://github.com/DrBaher/contract-lint-cli"
      icon="/assets/icons/contract-lint-cli.svg"
      version={meta['contract-lint-cli'].version}
      versionSource={meta['contract-lint-cli'].source}
      stars={meta['contract-lint-cli'].stars}
      weeklyDownloads={meta['contract-lint-cli'].weeklyDownloads}
      weeklyDownloadsSource={meta['contract-lint-cli'].weeklyDownloadsSource}
    />
    <ToolCard
      title="compare-cli"
      tagline="Clause-aware drift detection between two contract versions. Pre-signature gate with exit codes CI can branch on. No LLM tier."
      language="Node.js"
      install="npm i -g compare-cli"
      href="/tools/compare-cli/"
      github="https://github.com/DrBaher/compare-cli"
      icon="/assets/icons/compare-cli.svg"
      version={meta['compare-cli'].version}
      versionSource={meta['compare-cli'].source}
      stars={meta['compare-cli'].stars}
      weeklyDownloads={meta['compare-cli'].weeklyDownloads}
      weeklyDownloadsSource={meta['compare-cli'].weeklyDownloadsSource}
    />
    <ToolCard
      title="docx2pdf-cli"
      tagline="Honest DOCX → PDF conversion with batch processing, parallel runs, font validation, and pluggable backends."
      language="Node.js"
      install="npm i -g docx2pdf-cli"
      href="/tools/docx2pdf-cli/"
      github="https://github.com/DrBaher/docx2pdf-cli"
      icon="/assets/icons/docx2pdf-cli.svg"
      version={meta['docx2pdf-cli'].version}
      versionSource={meta['docx2pdf-cli'].source}
      stars={meta['docx2pdf-cli'].stars}
      weeklyDownloads={meta['docx2pdf-cli'].weeklyDownloads}
      weeklyDownloadsSource={meta['docx2pdf-cli'].weeklyDownloadsSource}
    />
    <ToolCard
      title="sign-cli"
      tagline="Fully-offline PAdES e-signature with hash-chained audit events, RFC 3161 timestamps, named profiles, and a 19-tool MCP server for agents."
      language="TypeScript"
      install="npx @drbaher/sign-cli@latest"
      href="/tools/sign-cli/"
      github="https://github.com/DrBaher/sign-cli"
      icon="/assets/icons/sign-cli.svg"
      version={meta['sign-cli'].version}
      versionSource={meta['sign-cli'].source}
      stars={meta['sign-cli'].stars}
      weeklyDownloads={meta['sign-cli'].weeklyDownloads}
      weeklyDownloadsSource={meta['sign-cli'].weeklyDownloadsSource}
    />
    <ToolCard
      title="contract-vault-cli"
      tagline="Post-signature layer: register signed contracts in a git-backed vault, then surface renewals, notice deadlines, and obligations as a queryable portfolio + an .ics calendar."
      language="Python"
      install="pipx install contract-vault"
      href="/tools/contract-vault-cli/"
      github="https://github.com/DrBaher/contract-vault-cli"
      icon="/assets/icons/contract-vault-cli.svg"
      version={meta['contract-vault-cli'].version}
      versionSource={meta['contract-vault-cli'].source}
      stars={meta['contract-vault-cli'].stars}
      weeklyDownloads={meta['contract-vault-cli'].weeklyDownloads}
      weeklyDownloadsSource={meta['contract-vault-cli'].weeklyDownloadsSource}
    />
  </div>

  <TryDemo
    href="https://contract-ops-playground-production.up.railway.app/?cli=nda-review"
    title="Try the NDA review live"
    blurb="Score an NDA against a house policy book and watch it flag every non-compliant clause, in a sandbox. No install. No sign-in."
  />

  <h2>Built for an agent-first workflow</h2>

  <p>
    Most legal-tech assumes a human at a desk: dashboards, threaded comments, in-app redlining.
    These CLIs assume the opposite — an LLM agent doing the operational work and a human approving
    the things that legitimately need a human. Drafting, scoring, suggesting amendments, sending,
    tracking: agent. Signing, escalating non-negotiable conflicts, accepting a final position:
    human, with a deliberate gesture.
  </p>

  <div class="not-prose my-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="rounded-lg border border-accent-200 bg-mint-50 p-4 dark:border-accent-700/40 dark:bg-accent-900/15">
      <div class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-accent-700 dark:text-accent-300">Agent does</div>
      <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1 text-[14px] text-ink-800 dark:text-night-100">
        <li>Drafts NDAs from your house templates</li>
        <li>Reviews counterparty docs against your policy</li>
        <li>Proposes amendments using your stance + priorities</li>
        <li>Sends documents for signature, tracks status</li>
        <li>Verifies signed PDFs and audit chains</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-lg border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 p-4 dark:border-amber-700/40 dark:bg-amber-900/15">
      <div class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-200">Human approves</div>
      <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1 text-[14px] text-ink-800 dark:text-night-100">
        <li>Signing — every signature requires a per-signer token</li>
        <li>Escalations on non-negotiable redlines</li>
        <li>Accepting the final agreed position before finalize</li>
        <li>Anything outside the deterministic policy guardrails</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>
    The MCP server in <a href="/tools/sign-cli/">sign-cli</a> exposes every command to any
    MCP-aware client (Claude Code, Cursor, Codex). Same per-signer guardrails — the agent never
    sees the approval token, the human does. <a href="/mcp/">Read the MCP guide</a> for the wire-up,
    or grab the hosted listing on <a href="https://smithery.ai/servers/drbaher/sign-cli" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Smithery</a> for one-click install into Claude Desktop, Cursor, and friends.
  </p>

  <h2>Why nine small tools instead of one big platform</h2>

  <p>
    Most contract operations products are SaaS suites. They want every step in one dashboard, every
    document in their database, every signature behind their identity provider. That's a fine
    business model for them, but it makes contract operations expensive, opaque, and — critically
    for an agent-first workflow — hard for an agent to drive without scraping or RPA glue.
  </p>

  <p>
    The nine CLIs here take the opposite stance. Each does one thing well. None of them require
    an account, a subscription, or a network call you didn't ask for. An agent can drive them over
    stdio or MCP; a human can drive them from a terminal. You can swap any one of them, fork them,
    or audit the source end to end. Together they cover the same workflow a SaaS suite would, with
    the documents and audit trail on your machine — and an interface an agent can use natively.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to go from here</h2>

  <ul>
    <li><a href="/tour/">5-minute tour</a> — run all nine zero-config demos, then chain them end to end. The fastest way in.</li>
    <li><a href="/workflow/">The workflow</a> — how the nine tools chain together, with copy-paste commands.</li>
    <li><a href="/install/">Install</a> — every install path on one page.</li>
    <li><a href="/mcp/">MCP guide</a> — drive the whole suite from an agent (Claude Code, Cursor, Codex).</li>
    <li><a href="/compare/">Comparison</a> — how the suite stacks up against SaaS contract platforms.</li>
    <li><a href="/principles/">Principles</a> — what these tools have in common and what they refuse to do.</li>
    <li><a href="/changelog/">Changelog</a> — what's new and what's coming next.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="text-[13px] text-ink-500 dark:text-night-200">Or jump straight to any tool from the cards above.</p>
</BaseLayout>
